{{~!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  courses/hero-variant.hbs — resolves a course's hero tag to ONE system class.

  Emits a bare class name and nothing else, so it drops straight into an
  attribute:

      <section class="ns-chero {{> "courses/hero-variant"}}">

  WHY A PARTIAL AND NOT AN INLINE {{#has}} CHAIN. The chain is eleven branches
  long and it is needed in three places on a course page — the hero itself,
  the decision to draw a background layer, and the decision to draw a media
  card. Written inline it would be copied three times and would disagree with
  itself the first time a variant was added.

  THE TAG CONTRACT — set ONE of these as an internal tag on the course post
  (Ghost Admin → the post → Tags → type `#hero-…`). Internal tags never appear
  on the site, which is why the theme uses them for art direction.

    #hero-console   brand navy + the hairline grid, media card beside.
                    THE DEFAULT — an untagged course renders this, which is
                    what every course rendered before the system landed.
    #hero-split     the same layout on the light surface. For a course whose
                    preview art carries the page better than the navy does.
    #hero-cover     a photographic still behind the copy, scrimmed. For a
                    course whose subject is visual.
    #hero-video     the same, with the intro lesson's poster as a play card.
    #hero-minimal   hairline and type only, no art. For a course with no good
                    image — which is most of them, and a blank grey box is
                    worse than no box.
    #hero-cert      the certification frame: the exam badge instead of art.

  NUMERIC ALIASES — KEEP THEM. Courses already published carry `#hero-1`..
  `#hero-5` from before the variants had names, and Ghost content is not in
  this repo, so a hard cutover would silently drop every one of those posts
  back to the default. Each numeric tag maps to the variant it used to draw:

    #hero-1 → console   navy, media beside              (the old default)
    #hero-2 → minimal   centred, no media               (loses the navy)
    #hero-3 → cover     media-led
    #hero-4 → minimal   compact, no media               (same shape as 2)
    #hero-5 → video     the intro-video poster

  Semantic tags are checked FIRST, so retagging a post in Ghost Admin takes
  effect even if the old numeric tag is still on it. Retag at leisure; delete
  this alias block only once no published course carries a numeric tag.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --~}}
{{~#has tag="#hero-console"}}ns-chero--console
{{~else has tag="#hero-split"}}ns-chero--split
{{~else has tag="#hero-cover"}}ns-chero--cover
{{~else has tag="#hero-video"}}ns-chero--video
{{~else has tag="#hero-minimal"}}ns-chero--minimal
{{~else has tag="#hero-cert"}}ns-chero--cert
{{~else has tag="#hero-1"}}ns-chero--console
{{~else has tag="#hero-2"}}ns-chero--minimal
{{~else has tag="#hero-3"}}ns-chero--cover
{{~else has tag="#hero-4"}}ns-chero--minimal
{{~else has tag="#hero-5"}}ns-chero--video
{{~else}}ns-chero--console
{{~/has~}}
